ule 110 and 184 are right-permutative.","optional_refs":[],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":[],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.1}],"scratch_proposal":{"unresolved_questions":[{"question":"For Rule 54, does the small-ring topology (W <= 11) destroy the complex glider interactions enough to force short cycles, or does it still violate the 4W bound like Rule 110?"}]},"simulation_proposals":[{"discriminating_purpose":"Compute the exact max transient and max cycle length over all 2^W initial states for rules 90, 110, 184, 54 and W in {5..11}, specifically distinguishing whether max(transient + cycle) exceeds 4*W.","hypothesis":"Exhaustive enumeration of finite state spaces for (rule, W) pairs will reveal that Rule 90 and Rule 184 always reach cycles of length ≤ 2 within 4W steps, while Rule 110 violates this for at least one width. Rule 54 is predicted to violate the bound for W=7, 9, or 11. The simulation returns the maximum transient length and cycle length for every pair.","interpretation_conditions":["The simulation must complete for all 2^W initial states.","The returned 'max_transient' and 'max_cycle' are exact maximums over the entire state space.","The 'all_short_cycles' observable evaluates the problem's specific bound: cycle <= 2 AND transient+cycle <= 4*W."],"model_source":"def simulate(inputs, rng):\n    rule = inputs['parameters']['rule']\n    W = inputs['parameters']['width']\n    rule_map = [(rule >> i) & 1 for i in range(8)]\n    \n    max_trans = 0\n    max_cycle = 0\n    witness_trans = []\n    \n    for init in range(1 << W):\n        state = [(init >> i) & 1 for i in range(W)]\n        visited = {}\n        seq = []\n        t = 0\n        while True:\n            key = tuple(state)\n            if key in visited:\n                cycle_len = t - visited[key]\n                trans_len = visited[key]\n                if trans_len > max_trans:\n                    max_trans = trans_len\n                    witness_trans = seq[:trans_len+1]\n                if cycle_len > max_cycle:\n                    max_cycle = cycle_len\n                break\n            visited[key] = t\n            seq.append(key)\n            nxt = [0]*W\n            for i in range(W):\n                l = state[(i-1)%W]\n                c = state[i]\n                r = state[(i+1)%W]\n                nxt[i] = rule_map[(l<<2)|(c<<1)|r]\n            state = nxt\n            t += 1\n            \n    return {\n        'max_transient': max_trans,\n        'max_cycle': max_cycle,\n        'all_short_cycles': max_trans + max_cycle <= 4 * W and max_cycle <= 2,\n        'witness': list(witness_trans[0]) if witness_trans else []\n    }","parameter_definitions":[{"name":"rule_width_pairs","values_json":"[{\"rule\": 90, \"width\": 5}, {\"rule\": 90, \"width\": 6}, {\"rule\": 90, \"width\": 7}, {\"rule\": 90, \"width\": 8}, {\"rule\": 90, \"width\": 9}, {\"rule\": 90, \"width\": 10}, {\"rule\": 90, \"width\": 11}, {\"rule\": 110, \"width\": 5}, {\"rule\": 110, \"width\": 6}, {\"rule\": 110, \"width\": 7}, {\"rule\": 110, \"width\": 8}, {\"rule\": 110, \"width\": 9}, {\"rule\": 110, \"width\": 10}, {\"rule\": 110, \"width\": 11}, {\"rule\": 184, \"width\": 5}, {\"rule\": 184, \"width\": 6}, {\"rule\": 184, \"width\": 7}, {\"rule\": 184, \"width\": 8}, {\"rule\": 184, \"width\": 9}, {\"rule\": 184, \"width\": 10}, {\"rule\": 184, \"width\": 11}, {\"rule\": 54, \"width\": 5}, {\"rule\": 54, \"width\": 6}, {\"rule\": 54, \"width\": 7}, {\"rule\": 54, \"width\": 8}, {\"rule\": 54, \"width\": 9}, {\"rule\": 54, \"width\": 10}, {\"rule\": 54, \"width\": 11}]"}],"request_identifier":"ca_short_cycle_enum","requested_observables":["max_transient","max_cycle","all_short_cycles","witness"],"rival_predictions":["Rule 110 reaches cycles ≤ 2 within 4W for all W.","Rule 90 or 184 violates the 4W bound for some W.","Rule 54 satisfies the bound for all W."],"simulation_mode":"sandboxed_python_v1"}]}